Z||000000||Denise||05-22-2000||12:44 PM||||OK it happend! yeah I know!  shoulda, coulda, woulda,  My F pump went on the night before I was to go to Carlise PA for the Car show! <BR> My Question is this... How, and what kind of external pump can be used on the car. and give us the 35lbs prssure needed with out being in the tank? But then. 13 yrs in gasoline is a good track record huh?<P>Denise Philly PA 86 SE 2.8 Jasper 5spd Iszsu||||reg||1
Z||000001||Gold-86SE||05-22-2000||12:50 PM||||<BR>Denise, first welcome to the forum and good to have as a member.<P>Second, why would you want an external pump, when replacement is fairly easy?<P>Please elaborate.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Denise||05-22-2000||01:09 PM||||Thanks Gold, I was just thinking and wondering. I like to know "things" that others are doing. We are installing a Delco OEM type pump.   <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Gold-86SE:<BR><B><BR>Denise, first welcome to the forum and good to have as a member.<P>Second, why would you want an external pump, when replacement is fairly easy?<P>Please elaborate.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>||||reg||10
Z||000003||theogre||05-22-2000||05:29 PM||||There really is no alternate if you have a tank pump than to replace it. in this case you've already chosen ACDelco which is the only sure choice for this particular part. This isn't a job to do twice.<P>replace the fuel filter and if it's at all beat looking, the sock on the pickup. Consider replacing the gauge sender while it's apart.||||reg||1
